# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# A Credential being written: Key Entry's temporary file, which exists between
# writing and renaming and would otherwise be an untracked secret that looks
# like an ordinary new file.
.key-entry-*.tmp

# Scratch directories left behind by a test run that did not clean up after
# itself. Credentials are written into temp projects during Key Entry tests, so
# a stray one must never be committable.
_tmp_*

# Scratch output. This repo is public, so a stray paste (an env dump, a log
# tail, a transcript) is permanent the moment it is pushed. Rather than
# enumerate the throwaway shapes and hope the list is complete, allowlist the
# three artifact types docs/agents/issue-tracker.md actually declares and let
# everything else default to untracked.
#
# Order matters: a file cannot be re-included while a parent directory of it
# is excluded, so each directory is re-included before the files within it.
.scratch/**
!.scratch/*/
!.scratch/*/spec.md
!.scratch/*/map.md
!.scratch/*/issues/
!.scratch/*/issues/**

# macOS AppleDouble resource forks (created when working on some volumes,
# including external SSDs). Vitest picks these up as broken test files.
._*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
